      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-card open">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>What is the average business loan interest rate in <%= currentYear %>?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            In 2026, SBA 7(a) variable rates average <strong>10.75% to 11.25%</strong> (WSJ Prime 8.50% + 2.25%–2.75%). Conventional bank term loans for prime established businesses range from <strong>7.50% to 12.00%</strong>. Equipment loans average 7.00% to 11.50%, and alternative online financing ranges from 15.00% to 35.00%+ APR.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>What credit score do I need for a commercial business loan?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Conventional bank term loans typically require a personal FICO score of <strong>680 to 720+</strong>. SBA 7(a) loans require a minimum 650 personal score and a FICO SBSS score of 155+. Online lenders may approve scores down to 600, though at higher interest rates.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>Is an SBA loan better than a conventional bank loan?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            SBA loans offer longer repayment terms (10 to 25 years) and lower down payment requirements (10% to 20%), resulting in lower monthly payments, but take 30 to 90 days to fund. Conventional bank loans close faster (2 to 4 weeks) with no SBA fees, but require shorter terms (3 to 7 years) and larger monthly payments.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>How does loan term affect total borrowing cost?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            A shorter loan term (e.g. 5 years) reduces total lifetime interest paid, but increases monthly cash flow drain. A longer term (e.g. 10 years) cuts monthly payments substantially, preserving working capital at the expense of higher cumulative interest.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>What is a Debt Service Coverage Ratio (DSCR) for business loans?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            DSCR measures your business cash flow capacity to service debt ($DSCR = Annual EBITDA / Annual P&I$). Commercial lenders typically require a minimum DSCR of <strong>1.20x to 1.35x</strong>.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>How much can my business borrow based on annual revenue?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Most commercial lenders cap maximum loan exposure at <strong>10% to 25% of annual gross sales</strong> or <strong>2.0x to 3.0x annual EBITDA</strong>, provided existing debt and operating margins demonstrate repayment stability.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>What documents are required to apply for a business loan?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Lenders require: 2–3 years of business tax returns, 2–3 years of personal tax returns for owners with 20%+ equity, year-to-date P&L and balance sheet, 6 months of bank statements, debt schedule, and articles of incorporation.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
          <button type="button" class="faq-trigger" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>Are commercial business loan interest payments tax deductible?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Yes. Interest paid on legitimate business loans used strictly for operational and capital needs is generally 100% tax-deductible as an ordinary business expense under IRS guidelines.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

